III. THE THIRD BOWL
Snow on the stair, snow on the bandage, snow on the road he came in by;
the stack is full this winter, and the bowls are full of red;
ah, the surgery lamp: it will not be put out tonight.
Brida had the first of them on the table before the gate was barred, a Keld archer with a crossbow bolt through the meat of the thigh. She cut the leather away.
